model {
  extend basalt.pool {
    metadata {
      constraint "The pool view keeps its existing bounded Home read without provider account inspection. Per-account native health is explicitly unavailable in this overview until a separate S2 path preserves exact-source permission outcomes within the 24-SELECT budget and passes its measured timing gate. History's first person-grouped series page receives at most 500 current pool members from one organization-and-audience constrained host directory read. Only hashes, names and current access are returned. Backend or browser directories cannot name people; continuation and non-person pages omit the directory. The legacy overview reuses the same authority helper. The summary exposes an observed retained start independently of selected-range capture. Its existing checkpoint SELECT reads at most 1001 rows in the earliest indexed timestamp bucket; an overfull bucket leaves the exact start unknown. This adds no SQL statement or ledger pricing pass, and never establishes import completion. Summary and capacity history share the existing maximum of 400 days. Settings' View all history opens the pool app's declared History page through the host's `page` parameter, the same tab Overview's own History tab shows, so History has one route and Back is the browser's. The pool app no longer posts a back message or renders its own header, tab bar or Back button; the host's older usage-history fragment still opens the App tab, where it now shows the overview. The overview drops its per-model limits and account-limits dialog; banked resets show per lab and kind, and per-model limits and spending stay on the host's Accounts tab; the native presentation journey checks the banked-reset list instead, and that the packaged pool view carries the provider's own available account view for its exact source account. The overview links to History only through the host page search: failed requests, a lab, and UTC dates. History parses only those keys, narrows its loaded records and lab groups in the page, and says the narrowing covers the requests read so far; the public reader has no account or failure filter."
    }
  }
}
